* {{this.projectCheckbox}} Fill in the project scope and objectives on the card *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.project}}"{{/xref}}* and then mark the page ready by using the "Activate" workflow transition.
* {{this.assignPeopleCheckbox}} *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.assignPeople}}"{{/xref}}* — Define who is responsible for security in the project. Without clear ownership, tasks will not get done.
* {{this.ensureCompetenceCheckbox}} *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.ensureCompetence}}"{{/xref}}* — Verify that assigned people have adequate cybersecurity knowledge, and arrange training where needed.
* {{this.documentSecurityContextCheckbox}} *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.documentSecurityContext}}"{{/xref}}* — Describe the product's operating environment, trust boundaries, and key security assumptions. This context guides threat modeling and requirements work.
* {{this.manageThreatModelsCheckbox}} *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.manageThreatModels}}"{{/xref}}* — Model your system's architecture and identify how it could be attacked. This reveals the risks and weaknesses that matter most.
* {{this.manageRisksCheckbox}} *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.manageRisks}}"{{/xref}}* - Identify and document risks for the entire product or for a specific asset
* {{this.securityRequirementsCheckbox}} *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.securityRequirements}}"{{/xref}}* — Turn identified risks into concrete security requirements that guide implementation and testing.
* {{this.processScopingCheckbox}} *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.processScoping}}"{{/xref}}* *Preform security controls scoping* — Go through security controls to perform risk based security controls scoping
* As development progresses, address controls in each subsequent phase.
* Use *{{#xref}}"cardKey": "{{this.statusNextSteps}}"{{/xref}}* to track overall progress and identify gaps.

TIP: You do not need to complete all phases at once. Start with Foundation and Design, then expand as your product matures.
